WEBVTT

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:44.480
Don't you see, Patricia?

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:47.940
If you leave on this train, then what happened between us is nothing but a dream.

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:49.220
Joseph!

00:01:51.510 --> 00:02:00.000
Do it, Patricia!

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.120
I love you, I love you.

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:04.770
And I will never forget you, my darling, never.

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:24.770
It's been an old movie, but I can see why your parents recommended it, Mamie.

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:26.600
It was so romantic, I thought I'd die.

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:30.000
Wouldn't it be great to be in love like that, where everything's really tragic?

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.900
and heartbreaking and you'd get to wear great outfits oh yeah that would be so

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:41.910
cool he looked a little like junior didn't you like it maybe huh oh yeah a

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:45.370
lot doesn't it make you want to fall in love with some super handsome guy and

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:53.400
break his heart yeah count me in

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:05.240
So how was the movie, girls?

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:07.480
So great!

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:08.900
It was the best!

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:11.090
A love story, a very sad one.

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:12.620
Really?

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:18.060
Yeah, these two people fall in love, but they're from totally different worlds, so at the end they have to break up.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:19.810
Goodbye, Joseph!

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:23.330
And you'd never believe how handsome the guy who played Joseph was.

00:03:23.330 --> 00:03:25.630
Huh?

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:28.520
Excuse me, but I think I'm about to be sick.

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:30.000
Oh, get out of here!

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.080
What business is it of yours anyway?

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:38.200
I'm always amazed about how you girls will go on and on about all this romantic and sappy nonsense.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:41.340
You wouldn't know true love if it bit you on the nose.

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:43.700
That's right, and I want to keep it that way.

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:49.600
Of course. Nobody expects you to know much about anything, Junior, because all you ever think about is Saint Tail.

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:50.600
I do not!

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:52.740
You've got Saint Tail on the brain!

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:53.940
What do you know?

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:55.540
More than you might think.

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:57.880
Forget it.

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:04.860
Maybe I overdid it.

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:15.640
That was quite a feat, traveling all over Japan by bicycle.

00:04:16.890 --> 00:04:21.690
Yeah, and I was on the last leg of my tour and about to go home to America when I met Minako here.

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:25.270
Oh, that's so romantic.

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:27.610
But then something happened that ruined it.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.020
Sounds like a great trip.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:49.340
Oh, it has been.

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:52.940
I've seen a lot of amazing things, but you know, I think this is my favorite spot.

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:54.470
Whoa, cool bike.

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:56.320
Why is that?

00:04:56.320 --> 00:04:57.320
Because I met you.

00:04:57.320 --> 00:04:58.360
Ah!

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:00.000
No, really, I mean it.

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:03.720
I was starting to get pretty lonely traveling by myself all the time.

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:06.430
Hey, listen, I don't have much time left here, so I was...

00:05:06.430 --> 00:05:07.730
Hmm?

00:05:07.730 --> 00:05:09.600
That's my bike!

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:14.170
Where do you think you're going?

00:05:14.170 --> 00:05:15.400
Come back here!

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:43.720
Wait, sir. Hey, pal, what do you think you're doing?

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:45.820
Open this gate! Let me in there!

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:53.870
John, what in the world is all this ruckus?

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:55.170
Sorry about that, ma'am.

00:05:55.510 --> 00:05:57.990
This gentleman was demanding that I open up the gate for him.

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:01.690
Hmm...

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:05.840
Excuses for disturbing you. We just saw a little boy ride John's bike in here.

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:08.240
Are you implying Tatsuo took your bike?

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:10.250
That's exactly what he did.

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:16.100
Is this some kind of joke? He already has a very expensive bicycle of his own.

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:17.900
I really don't think he would want yours.

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:20.500
Please, it's got my name on it on the rear fender.

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:22.200
Won't you please take a look at least?

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:26.400
No, I will not! Nor will I stand here and listen to you accuse Tatsuo of thievery!

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:28.200
Kindly leave this instant!

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:31.030
I see.

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:34.690
We went back a couple of times, but no one would come out, and the place was locked up

00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:35.690
tight.

00:06:35.690 --> 00:06:39.630
And John doesn't want to get the little boy into any serious trouble by going to the police.

00:06:39.630 --> 00:06:41.300
That bike and I had been everywhere.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:45.420
It was like having a best friend who traveled all over the world with me, who was always

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:49.960
there in good times and bad.

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:54.300
All we can really do now is wait and hope the boy comes to his senses and returns it.

00:06:54.300 --> 00:07:00.000
Yes, if we're patient, and if we pray hard, I'm certain that a solution

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:08.080
to our problem will make itself known i bet john and minako are really in love huh they seem very

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:14.830
fond of each other it's so romantic their love will shine like the brightest flame and end in

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:22.520
heartbreak when they're parted forever whoa maybe let's not get carried away consider it done sarah

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:28.970
i'm on the case the only problem is we don't have much time john's flying back to america tonight we

00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:30.000
have to get his bicycle parked

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:33.010
back before then. If not, it'll be too late.

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:39.510
Ha-ha! Never fear for St. Tal, the protector of young lovers everywhere is on the job!

00:07:39.510 --> 00:07:42.070
What's come over her?

00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:49.780
Dad can be such a pain. Every Thursday night it has to be the same boring stuff.

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:55.530
Ah, my favorite. At least I could spice it up with this.

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:58.430
Huh?

00:07:58.430 --> 00:08:00.000
Tonight I'll be at the Ninomiya residence.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.520
Stealing a bicycle, St. Tail.

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:12.160
Ugh, the weird thing is how did St. Tail know this stuff's my favorite?

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:16.390
Very good, I'm really impressed.

00:08:22.870 --> 00:08:24.680
Wow, that's amazing, Ruby.

00:08:27.220 --> 00:08:29.600
Mamie, it's time for dinner.

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:32.950
Okay!

00:08:32.950 --> 00:08:34.580
Oh!

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:39.520
Mmm, smells yummy-licious!

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:40.560
Huh?

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:42.680
Eeeegg!

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:07.800
There! She can be the world's first flying hedgehog!

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:10.290
I like it!

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:13.770
Nice trick! You should put her in your next performance!

00:09:13.770 --> 00:09:17.250
Hey! Wanna be in my magic show, Ruby?

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:35.380
Yeah, he sure got a lot of toys.

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:38.820
I got a lot more.

00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:40.180
Take anything you want.

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:42.690
Thanks.

00:09:42.690 --> 00:09:44.620
Where's the bicycle in question?

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:46.700
Right over there.

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:51.120
Yeah, go on and borrow it if you want.

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:52.950
You can keep it, I don't care.

00:09:52.950 --> 00:09:56.850
I thought it was some kind of super special bike.

00:09:56.850 --> 00:09:58.320
Eh, not really.

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:01.250
Oh, is that right?

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:04.800
Well, if that's the way you feel, we might as well give it to that bothersome young fellow

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:06.630
who keeps coming to the gate.

00:10:06.630 --> 00:10:12.100
Uh, uh, I was just joking.

00:10:12.100 --> 00:10:16.240
I have a dinner party that I absolutely cannot miss, so I'll leave the situation in your

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:17.240
hands.

00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:19.410
Ta-ta!

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:25.320
Hmm.

00:10:25.320 --> 00:10:30.000
Tatsuo, why would Saint Teo want to steal this kid's body?

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:44.950
By glow of the moon or light of the sun, it's time to do what must be done.

00:11:12.670 --> 00:11:14.970
Remember, in order for John to make his flight tonight,

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:17.470
he'll have to take the 9 o'clock shuttle from the train station,

00:11:17.590 --> 00:11:18.610
so you mustn't be late.

00:11:19.450 --> 00:11:20.490
The 9 o'clock train.

00:11:20.830 --> 00:11:21.730
Right, I got it.

00:11:24.230 --> 00:11:27.490
May fortune smile on us in our efforts to do good deeds.

00:11:48.620 --> 00:11:54.360
Junior's not making this easy.

00:12:02.810 --> 00:12:07.270
Okay, I want someone guarding the door to this room and every possible entrance to the house.

00:12:07.270 --> 00:12:10.190
Yes, sir!

00:12:10.190 --> 00:12:28.290
Huh? It's what?

00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:42.960
- What's happening?

00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:49.830
- Huh?

00:12:49.830 --> 00:13:00.000
- Huh?

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:30.000
know who's not very nice what are you talking about oh I think you're kidding me it's not your

00:13:30.030 --> 00:13:40.430
All right, come out of there, St. Tale!

00:13:40.430 --> 00:13:41.430
Nuh-uh!

00:13:41.430 --> 00:13:45.440
Huh?

00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:46.440
Not again!

00:13:46.440 --> 00:13:50.340
What's going on?

00:13:50.340 --> 00:13:51.420
Okay, stay calm.

00:13:51.420 --> 00:13:54.420
One of you check the box and see if we've blown a fuse.

00:13:54.420 --> 00:13:55.320
Right!

00:13:55.320 --> 00:13:58.130
Huh?

00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:14.550
This is the second floor!

00:14:14.550 --> 00:14:27.060
Three!

00:14:27.060 --> 00:14:30.000
I've never seen a bicycle fly before.

00:14:30.190 --> 00:14:32.690
Well, I wish I could say it was all magic.

00:14:32.690 --> 00:14:42.000
Let the wind carry me to the train station!

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:46.650
Huh?

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:53.020
You're not thinking of...

00:14:53.020 --> 00:14:57.590
Hurry up and bring the car around!

00:15:01.180 --> 00:15:04.100
- This is not how I planned it.

00:15:04.100 --> 00:15:10.510
I've got an extra balloon here somewhere.

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:23.000
- Your luck's run out, I've gotcha.

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:23.940
I made it.

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:26.100
Not bad, huh?

00:15:26.100 --> 00:15:27.700
- Oscar Junior, sir, look out.

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:29.860
- Huh?

00:15:55.310 --> 00:15:57.330
You look pretty from up here.

00:15:57.330 --> 00:16:00.000
You don't.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:05.210
Oh, brother, I've got to get rid of him.

00:16:05.210 --> 00:16:11.630
Hey, hey, what's going on?

00:16:11.630 --> 00:16:16.350
Get off me.

00:16:16.350 --> 00:16:17.350
Not on your life.

00:16:17.350 --> 00:16:18.670
Uh.

00:16:18.670 --> 00:16:21.450
Uh.

00:16:21.450 --> 00:16:22.450
Uh.

00:16:22.450 --> 00:16:23.240
Uh.

00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:34.590
I need to borrow your bike!

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:36.210
Uh, yes, sir. Thanks.

00:16:36.210 --> 00:16:49.450
Can you tell me what time it is?

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:51.900
Sure, it's about 10 minutes before 9:00.

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:53.240
Thanks a lot!

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:57.010
What was that?!

00:17:00.760 --> 00:17:03.230
Huh?

00:17:03.230 --> 00:17:22.560
They're all night! You're not getting away from me!

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:26.570
Ugh!

00:17:26.570 --> 00:17:28.680
Hatsuo's name tag?

00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:33.980
Hmm?

00:17:33.980 --> 00:17:36.350
Hey, wait! Who in the heck is John?

00:17:36.350 --> 00:17:53.910
There are times I really wonder about this line of work.

00:18:00.670 --> 00:18:04.390
Hate to disappoint you, Missy, but you don't get rid of me that easily!

00:18:08.880 --> 00:18:11.490
When he chases me...

00:18:11.490 --> 00:18:12.420
Hmm?

00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:21.550
I'm running out of time!

00:18:21.550 --> 00:18:24.790
Huh?

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:26.280
The train station?

00:18:26.280 --> 00:18:27.570
Huh?

00:18:27.570 --> 00:18:29.030
Huh?

00:18:31.400 --> 00:18:36.820
Oh, now that hurt. Huh?

00:18:36.820 --> 00:18:41.050
I think I have about two stops.

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:47.230
Get on and then...

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:49.670
I wish you'd come to the airport.

00:18:49.670 --> 00:18:53.950
I can't, John. It'll just make saying goodbye that much harder.

00:18:53.950 --> 00:18:57.520
John? Is that the John? The bike John?

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:04.000
Even though all this meant losing my bicycle, I wouldn't change a thing.

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:06.140
Neither would I.

00:19:06.140 --> 00:19:08.580
Ah!

00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:12.270
Wow, I can't believe it!

00:19:12.270 --> 00:19:15.660
It's your bike, all right, but how on earth did it get here?

00:19:15.660 --> 00:19:18.810
Our prayers were answered. It doesn't matter how.

00:19:18.810 --> 00:19:21.610
John, we'll see each other again, won't we?

00:19:21.610 --> 00:19:24.480
You can bet on it.

00:19:24.480 --> 00:19:28.850
Look, I never thought I'd see my bike again, but it's like we were meant to be together.

00:19:28.850 --> 00:19:30.000
You and me?

00:19:30.190 --> 00:19:31.410
We're meant to be together.

00:19:33.870 --> 00:19:44.050
It was so sweet.

00:19:46.750 --> 00:19:53.830
That's what this was all about.

00:20:01.720 --> 00:20:16.950
Oh, it's you, Mamie.

00:20:16.950 --> 00:20:18.950
What's the problem? Something got you down?

00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:22.740
Huh? Leave me alone, will ya? You wouldn't understand.

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:25.740
Well, how do you know if you won't even tell me about it, huh?

00:20:25.740 --> 00:20:27.740
Oh, it's all this dumb love stuff.

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:28.230
Huh?

00:20:31.210 --> 00:20:32.840
to tell me you've fallen in love?

00:20:32.840 --> 00:20:34.160
Huh? Not me.

00:20:34.160 --> 00:20:36.660
Huh?

00:20:36.660 --> 00:20:37.660
We're gonna be late.

00:20:37.660 --> 00:20:38.660
Race ya!

00:20:38.660 --> 00:20:44.660
This time, maybe I'll let him win.

00:22:31.530 --> 00:22:39.490
I want to pick up a doll from a girl and give it back to her, but she's hiding it in a park in the neighborhood, in the name of Little.

00:22:39.490 --> 00:22:44.600
And on top of that, there's a stolen jewel in the doll's belly.

00:22:44.600 --> 00:22:47.620
It's getting more and more complicated.

00:22:47.620 --> 00:22:51.480
Let's get rid of the jewel thief!

00:22:51.480 --> 00:22:52.990
Maken Little!

00:22:52.990 --> 00:22:55.920
May everyone have the protection of God!
